---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navbar from '../../components/Navbar.astro';
import PageShell from '../../components/PageShell.astro';
---

<Layout 
    title="Editorial Policy & Reference Standards | Real BMI"
    description="Read our editorial policy for evidence-based health content, peer-reviewed methodology, clinical screening definitions, and transparent user guidance."
>
    <Navbar />
    <PageShell
      title="Editorial Policy"
      eyebrow="Methodology & Transparency"
      description="How Bhawanshi Dosi researches, references, and maintains evidence-based health tools and educational content."
      returnUrl="/en/"
      returnLabel="Home"
    >
      <div class="space-y-8 prose prose-zinc dark:prose-invert max-w-none text-[var(--muted-foreground)] leading-relaxed text-lg font-medium">
        <p>Welcome to <strong>Real BMI</strong>. This website is run by <strong>Bhawanshi Dosi</strong> in Banswara, Rajasthan, India. Our goal is to provide clear, reliable health calculators for everyone. We help you check your body mass index, resting calories, daily burn, and other key body numbers. We believe that health math should be simple and open to all.</p>

        <h2>1. Evidence-Based Guidelines</h2>
        <p>All formulas and health ranges on our site come from trusted global health groups. These include:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>World Health Organization (WHO):</strong> Global obesity cutoffs, Asian BMI ranges (23.0 kg/m²), and waist-to-hip ratio guides.</li>
          <li><strong>Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC):</strong> Adult BMI formulas and child growth percentile charts.</li>
          <li><strong>National Institutes of Health (NIH):</strong> Body surface area and metabolic burn formulas.</li>
          <li><strong>Published Medical Research:</strong> Proven math formulas from scientists like Mifflin-St Jeor, Harris-Benedict, Boer, Devine, and Mosteller.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>2. Author Identity &amp; Standards</h2>
        <p>Real BMI is an independent website run with full openness:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Founder &amp; Developer:</strong> <strong>Bhawanshi Dosi</strong> manages all coding, formula math, unit tests, and website design. No personal data is ever saved or shared.</li>
          <li><strong>Tested Formulas:</strong> Each calculator is a clean implementation of published health math. We test both metric and imperial units with automated code checks.</li>
          <li><strong>Non-Clinical Resource:</strong> Real BMI is an educational website. It is not a clinic, hospital, or doctor review board. Our calculators provide general health awareness and do not replace medical advice.</li>
          <li><strong>Direct User Feedback:</strong> We welcome questions, math corrections, and research papers from readers and doctors through our <a href="/en/contact/" class="text-[var(--accent)] underline font-medium">contact page</a>.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>3. Openness &amp; Regular Updates</h2>
        <p>We review health guidelines often. When health groups update their guidelines, we update our calculators and guides to match. Each article lists its citations and sources clearly. We never use hidden formulas. You can see the math behind every result. We keep every equation simple and clear.</p>

        <h2>4. Independent &amp; Ad-Safe Content</h2>
        <p>Real BMI is an independent project. No drug companies or advertisers tell us what to write. Our math remains fair and objective. We never accept sponsored results or paid rankings. Every calculation uses the exact same medical formula for all visitors.</p>

        <h2>5. Educational Disclaimer</h2>
        <p>All results on this site are for learning and planning only. We do not offer medical diagnosis, treatments, or prescriptions. Always speak with your doctor or healthcare provider about any health concern. Never ignore medical advice because of something you read on this site.</p>

        <h2>6. Review Cycle &amp; Fact Checks</h2>
        <p>We check all formulas and tables twice a year. When groups like the WHO or CDC publish new data, we check our tools against their whitepapers. We run automated tests before every release to guarantee math precision. Over 920 unit tests run on our codebase every day.</p>

        <h2>7. Human Authorship</h2>
        <p>All guides, worked examples, step-by-step math steps, and FAQs are written originally by Bhawanshi Dosi using primary health sources. We do not publish automated AI text without human review. Every word is checked for clarity and accuracy. We write in plain English so that all readers can follow along easily.</p>

        <h2>8. Corrections Policy</h2>
        <p>We care about accuracy. If you spot a math mistake, an unclear term, or an old link, please tell us on our <a href="/en/contact/" class="text-[var(--accent)] underline font-medium">contact page</a>. We review all reports quickly and update our live code within 24 to 48 hours. We keep a full history of all code changes in our project records.</p>

        <h2>9. Content Review &amp; Privacy Checks</h2>
        <p>Every calculator and guide goes through four checks before going live:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Step 1: Source check.</strong> We verify formulas against WHO and CDC papers.</li>
          <li><strong>Step 2: Math test.</strong> We test edge cases in both metric and imperial units.</li>
          <li><strong>Step 3: Privacy check.</strong> We make sure no personal data or names are ever collected or stored.</li>
          <li><strong>Step 4: Final review.</strong> We check formatting, links, and text clarity.</li>
        </ul>
      
        <h2>10. Ethical Advertising &amp; Public Health Mission</h2>
        <p>To keep all 23 health tools completely free for individuals, students, educators, and community health workers worldwide, Real BMI is funded through non-intrusive digital advertisements served via Google AdSense. We enforce strict editorial firewalls. No advertiser, pharmaceutical company, or supplement manufacturer exercises any editorial influence over our mathematical algorithms, diagnostic disclosures, or educational articles. Our math remains strictly objective, evidence-based, and calibrated directly to international public health literature.</p>

        <h2>11. Automated Testing Pipeline</h2>
        <p>We do not use a doctor panel. Instead, we achieve accuracy through strict software testing. Every formula, conversion factor, and cutoff boundary is verified by an automated test suite. We run over 920 automated tests before every update. These tests check metric and imperial parity with a strict tolerance of 0.01. They also test extreme boundary inputs to ensure math stability.</p>

        <h2>12. Zero-Retention Privacy Architecture</h2>
        <p>Your privacy is our top priority. All calculations run 100% inside your web browser. When you enter your height, weight, or age, those numbers never leave your device. We do not send your data to any remote server. We do not store health numbers in cookies or local storage. You can even use our calculators when your device is offline.</p>

        <h2>13. Cultural Context &amp; Asian Health Standards</h2>
        <p>Standard WHO BMI cutoffs were originally developed using Western populations. Research shows that South Asian and East Asian populations often face higher health risks at lower BMI levels. To respect these differences, Real BMI includes specialized tools with Asian risk cutoffs (23.0 kg/m² for overweight, 27.5 kg/m² for obesity) based on WHO Western Pacific and ICMR guidelines.</p>

        <h2>14. Clear Non-Diagnostic Boundaries</h2>
        <p>Our calculators provide mathematical estimates based on public research. They are not medical diagnostic tools. Many health factors, such as muscle mass, bone density, hydration, and medical history, cannot be captured by simple height and weight inputs. We always encourage users to share their results with qualified medical professionals for comprehensive health evaluations.</p>

        <h2>15. Open Science &amp; Global Accessibility</h2>
        <p>We believe that evidence-based health tools should be free and accessible to everyone worldwide. We maintain all 23 computational health tools across six global languages: English, Spanish, French, German, Korean, and Hindi. Every page includes full mathematical documentation, clear formulas, worked examples, and direct links to primary scientific citations.</p>
      </div>
    </PageShell>
</Layout>
